QMacStyle: Inset the text of line edits like NSTextField under Liquid Glass

Not upstream, applies on top of qtbase-macstyle-textfield-heights.patch.
QMacStyle in the 6.10, 6.11 and 6.12 branches and in dev (checked in
November 2026) has no Liquid Glass insets for the text of line edits.

With Liquid Glass a bezeled NSTextField keeps its text 7.5 to 8 pt away
from the outer edge of its bezel at either side, for every control
size; the bezel reaches 1 pt beyond the frame of the text field, while
QMacStyle draws it inside the rect of a line edit. A line edit started
its text 2.5 to 3 pt from the edge of the bezel and, aligned to the end,
ended it 5.5 to 6.5 pt before the other edge, and so did the edit field
of a spin box. A line edit with a frame and the edit field of a spin box
with a frame now keep 5 pt more at the start of the text and 2 pt more
at its end, mirrored for right-to-left, which puts the text within half
a point of where AppKit has it. Their size hints grow by the same 7 pt,
so that what fitted before still fits, like the widest value of a spin
box. Frameless line edits, like editors in item views and the line edit
of an editable combo box, are left as they are. Only Liquid Glass is
affected.

--- a/qtbase/src/plugins/styles/mac/qmacstyle_mac.mm
+++ b/qtbase/src/plugins/styles/mac/qmacstyle_mac.mm
@@ -370,6 +370,14 @@
     26, 24, 21
 };
 
+// Room added between the bezel and the text of a line edit with Liquid Glass,
+// where the text starts and where it ends. A bezeled NSTextField keeps its text
+// 7.5 to 8 pt away from the outer edge of the bezel at either side, the same
+// for every control size, while a line edit starts it 2.5 to 3 pt from the
+// edge and, aligned to the end, ends it 5.5 to 6.5 pt before the other edge.
+static const int textFieldLiquidGlassTextLeading = 5;
+static const int textFieldLiquidGlassTextTrailing = 2;
+
 static const int toolButtonArrowSize = 7;
 static const int toolButtonArrowMargin = 2;
 
@@ -5220,6 +5228,24 @@
         else
 #endif
             rect.adjust(-1, -1, 0, +1);
+        if (qt_apple_runningWithLiquidGlass()) {
+            // A line edit with a frame is drawn as a bezeled NSTextField, and so
+            // is a spin box with a frame, whose edit field is a frameless line
+            // edit over the bezel. Their text keeps the distance from the bezel
+            // that NSTextField keeps.
+            const auto *frame = qstyleoption_cast<const QStyleOptionFrame *>(opt);
+            bool bezeled = frame && frame->lineWidth > 0;
+#if QT_CONFIG(spinbox)
+            if (const auto *spinBox = widget ? qobject_cast<const QAbstractSpinBox *>(widget->parentWidget()) : nullptr)
+                bezeled = spinBox->hasFrame();
+#endif
+            if (bezeled) {
+                if (opt->direction == Qt::RightToLeft)
+                    rect.adjust(textFieldLiquidGlassTextTrailing, 0, -textFieldLiquidGlassTextLeading, 0);
+                else
+                    rect.adjust(textFieldLiquidGlassTextLeading, 0, -textFieldLiquidGlassTextTrailing, 0);
+            }
+        }
         break;
     case SE_CheckBoxLayoutItem:
         rect = opt->rect;
@@ -6627,6 +6653,8 @@
             if (vopt->frame && qt_apple_runningWithLiquidGlass()) {
                 const auto size = d->effectiveAquaSizeConstrain(opt, widget);
                 sz.setHeight(qMax(sz.height(), textFieldLiquidGlassHeight[size]));
+                // Room for the text insets of the edit field (see SE_LineEditContents)
+                sz.rwidth() += textFieldLiquidGlassTextLeading + textFieldLiquidGlassTextTrailing;
             }
         }
         break;
@@ -6642,6 +6670,8 @@
             if (frame && frame->lineWidth > 0) {
                 const auto size = d->effectiveAquaSizeConstrain(opt, widget, ct);
                 sz.setHeight(qMax(sz.height(), textFieldLiquidGlassHeight[size]));
+                // Room for the text insets (see SE_LineEditContents)
+                sz.rwidth() += textFieldLiquidGlassTextLeading + textFieldLiquidGlassTextTrailing;
                 useAquaGuideline = false;
             }
         }
